id: pm-hen0t6
title: "Replay each history state once: reuse the previous entry's digest as the next before-hash, stop at the first matching hash epoch, and drop the second document clone"
description: "First tranche of pm-29ymfn. Chain verification canonicalized and digested every replayed state twice (as one entry's after state and the next entry's before state), evaluated every supported hash epoch for unversioned entries even after the preferred epoch matched, and cloned each document twice per entry because fast-json-patch deep-cloned a document the caller had already structured-cloned. Constant-factor only: the quadratic growth for living items remains owned by the parent."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: "area:history",performance
created_at: "2026-09-28T15:28:58.808Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-28T16:01:18.194Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-28T16:01:18.159Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-28T16:01:18.159Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "verifyHistoryChainWithVersion returns byte-identical results to the published 2026.9.28 build for every stream in this workspace and for deterministic corruptions (changed after_hash, changed before_hash, tampered patch value, deleted entry); A digest is reused only for the same document, hash epoch and digest algorithm; a regression spec forges a before_hash with the other algorithm's valid digest of the same state and is refused, and fails when the algorithm is dropped from the memo key; Full coverage, lint and typecheck gates stay green"
parent: pm-29ymfn
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Memoized before-digests from the previous entry's after-digests keyed by hash epoch and algorithm, evaluated hash epochs lazily in preference order, and removed fast-json-patch's redundant deep clone of an already private structured clone."
expected_result: "Each replayed history state is canonicalized and digested once per hash epoch and algorithm, with verdicts byte-identical to the previous implementation."
actual_result: "In-process verification of all 2,846 streams 110.5 s to 33.9 s; validate --check-history-drift 98.8 s to about 41 s. Verdicts byte-identical to published 2026.9.28 on every stream and 949 deterministic corruptions. New algorithm-reuse negative control fails when the algorithm is dropped from the memo key. Full coverage 750 files and 9,393 tests green at 100 percent thresholds; quality:static green; 216 history-related spec files (4,231 tests) green."
